# Gapless fast path: warm start (no start-of-track muting for a retained decoder).
name: gapless-warm-start
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03051504
gate: build refuses unless the 16 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: After every track start the playback monitor (0x03064F7E, the
  decoder core's channel 14 callback) zeroes the first three decoded
  buffers and restores the volume on the fourth (counter at 0x0304AD84,
  reset to 0 by module 34's start routine at 0x0308C2A2). That is
  Rockchip's AudioErrorFrameNum logic (SDK Service.c), which hides a
  cold decoder's start-up output; on a natural advance it is 3 buffers of
  silence (about 80 ms for MP3, up to about 280 ms for 4,096-sample FLAC
  frames), by far the largest part of the gap. When the gate (0022)
  retains the decoder, the decoder is warm and its first output is
  real audio, so the gate's retained path now branches here: it stores
  module | 0x80 to the state word as before, then sets the counter to 3.
  The monitor's next call counts to 4, restores the saved volume (the
  value already set) and zeroes nothing. Cold starts, skips and codec
  changes take the gate's miss path and keep stock behaviour. Occupies
  four verified-dead `bx lr` stubs of the module 0 stub farm (the span
  the retired delay cave freed; patches/framework/space_budget.md).
  Bytes: patches/gapless/tools/assemble_v2.py.
